An import loaded product codes into `staging(code varchar(10))` with the rows `'AB12'`, `'ab12'` and `'AB12 '` (trailing space). `products(code varchar(10))` holds one row, `'AB12'`. In PostgreSQL, how many rows does each query return?

```sql
-- Q1
SELECT * FROM staging s JOIN products p ON s.code = p.code;
-- Q2
SELECT * FROM staging s JOIN products p ON trim(s.code) = p.code;
-- Q3
SELECT * FROM staging s JOIN products p ON lower(trim(s.code)) = lower(p.code);
```
